fix(codegen-rust): bind index in `for v, i in xs` loops
scale: ~15 lines across 1 files [S]

- `crates/vox-codegen/src/codegen_rust/emit/stmt_expr_tail.rs`: Modified the code generation for `HirExpr::For` loops to correctly handle indexed forms (`for v, i in xs`).
  - When an index is present, the generated Rust code now uses `.into_iter().enumerate()` on the iterable.
  - The index variable is explicitly shadowed as an `i64` (corresponding to Vox `int`) to ensure type-checking within the loop body.
  - This resolves `E0425` errors where the index variable `i` was undefined in the emitted Rust.

